From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:12:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 34/39] spu: drop the Report property from the option records
 the patch series adds (removed in GCC 11)

---
 gcc/config/spu/spu.opt | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu.opt b/gcc/config/spu/spu.opt
index 063668cb3b5..64d9091ae08 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu.opt
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu.opt
@@ -48,19 +48,19 @@ Target Mask(STD_MAIN)
 Use standard main function as entry for startup.
 
 mspurs-job
-Target Report RejectNegative
+Target RejectNegative
 Build as a SPURS Job 2.0 binary (without job CRT). Sets ELF e_flags=1.
 
 mspurs-job-initialize
-Target Report RejectNegative
+Target RejectNegative
 Build as a SPURS Job 2.0 binary with job CRT. Sets ELF e_flags=2.
 
 mspurs-task
-Target Report RejectNegative
+Target RejectNegative
 Build as a SPURS Task binary. Sets ELF e_flags=3.
 
 mcustom-module
-Target Report RejectNegative
+Target RejectNegative
 Build a position-independent image for a custom SPURS policy module to load: linked at 0 with a fixup table that _init applies.
 
 mbranch-hints
